ed_by_judge": "Verify the accepted objective set no longer contains 'quality_score' and that next-iteration selection/offspring statistics are driven by parameter_mean and parameter_spread. Confirm no further runs are dominated by extremely large objective values and that population metrics (parameter_mean/spread) continue to show plausible improvement.", "self_reported_confidence_uncalibrated": 0.86}, "notes": [], "judge_raw_output": "Reasoning: the analyzer shows quality_score values are massively out of range (mean = 465,965,998, best = 485,165,195) vs documented [0,1], so that objective currently dominates multi-objective selection and will mislead the optimizer. We cannot rebuild the scorer here; the least-risk immediate fix is to remove the faulty objective so the optimizer continues using the sane parameter objectives (parameter_mean and parameter_spread) until the scorer is corrected.\n\n<decision>\n{\n  \"failure_location\": \"implementation\",\n  \"root_cause_hypothesis\": \"The registered 'quality_score' scorer is returning wildly scaled values (mean = 465,965,998; best = 485,165,195) instead of values in [0,1], indicating a scorer implementation/scaling bug.\",\n  \"intervention_target\": \"objective\",\n  \"rationale\": \"Quality_score values (mean 465,965,998 \u00b1 60,633,639, best 485,165,195) vastly exceed the documented [0,1] range and will dominate selection. Removing the objective is a minimal, reversible intervention that prevents misleading selection pressure while leaving parameter_mean (mean = 0.6857 \u00b1 0.0828) and parameter_spread (mean = 0.3476 \u00b1 0.0735) to guide optimization.\",\n  \"proposed_change\": {\n    \"ops\": [\n      {\n        \"op\": \"drop\",\n        \"name\": \"quality_score\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"expected_benefit\": \"Removes the distorted influence of the mis-scaled quality_score so the optimizer will make selection decisions based on parameter_mean and parameter_spread (both behaving in expected ranges), reducing risk of optimizing toward artifacts of a buggy scorer and preserving productive search.\",\n  \"validation_plan\": \"Verify the accepted objective set no longer contains 'quality_score' and that next-iteration selection/offspring statistics are driven by parameter_mean and parameter_spread. Confirm no further runs are dominated by extremely large objective values and that population metrics (parameter_mean/spread) continue to show plausible improvement.\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.86\n}\n</decision>", "change_id": "5dd52069c8cc2fa4", "candidate_state": {"version": 0, "planner_guidance": null, "objective_ops": [{"op": "drop", "name": "quality_score"}], "implementation_patches": {}, "workflow_params": {}}, "validation": {"seeds": [2000, 2001], "use_planner": false, "candidate_objectives": ["parameter_mean", "parameter_spread"], "baseline_objectives": ["quality_score", "parameter_mean", "parameter_spread"], "baseline": [2.908626999346927e-05, 1.8324772706774525e-05], "candidate": [1.6679515424036412e-06, 1.350935706069599e-06], "baseline_mean": 2.3705521350121898e-05, "candidate_mean": 1.50944362423662e-06, "delta": -2.2196077725885277e-05, "min_improvement": 0.02, "candidate_constraint_violation": false, "details": {"baseline": [{"split": "validation", "top_k": 5, "top_k_by_true_quality": 0.0007641770032672157, "population_mean": 0.00016921087294879034, "best": 0.0018865623803412921, "n_invalid": 0}, {"split": "validation", "top_k": 5, "top_k_by_true_quality": 6.868481513434095e-05, "population_mean": 2.0781026542829146e-05, "best": 0.00011357278887509042, "n_invalid": 0}], "candidate": [{"split": "validation", "top_k": 5, "top_k_by_true_quality": 7.068922207161434e-06, "population_mean": 3.751505207515613e-06, "best": 7.52019598311603e-06, "n_invalid": 0}, {"split": "validation", "top_k": 5, "top_k_by_true_quality": 6.816515491192634e-06, "population_mean": 2.814162125144917e-06, "best": 1.1088339659644812e-05, "n_invalid": 0}]}}, "outcome": "rejected", "reason": 